Embed/hold the underlying `io.Reader` and implement `Read` to delegate and accumulate:

```go
type CountingReader struct {
    R io.Reader
    N int64
}
func (c *CountingReader) Read(p []byte) (int, error) {
    n, err := c.R.Read(p)
    c.N += int64(n)
    return n, err
}
```

Because it *is* an `io.Reader`, it drops into `io.Copy`, `bufio.NewReader`, `json.NewDecoder`, etc. unchanged. This 'decorator over a small interface' pattern is the heart of idiomatic Go composition — exactly what interviewers want to see instead of inheritance.
